---
import {frame} from './model.mjs';
import './figures.css';
const {kind,number,title,caption}=Astro.props;
const first=frame(kind);
---
<figure class="ix-figure wide" data-index-figure data-kind={kind} aria-labelledby={`ix-title-${kind}`}>
 <figcaption id={`ix-title-${kind}`}><span>Figure {number}</span><strong>{title}</strong></figcaption>
 <div class="ix-panel">
  {kind==='keys'&&<label class="ix-choice">Index key <select data-option="variant" aria-label="Index key"><option value="customer">Customer only</option><option value="history" selected>Customer, then time and ID</option><option value="time">Time, then customer and ID</option></select></label>}
  {kind==='locality'&&<div class="ix-choices"><label class="ix-choice">Table layout <select data-option="layout" aria-label="Table layout"><option value="scattered">Mixed customers</option><option value="grouped">By customer</option></select></label><label class="ix-choice">Match customers <select data-option="maximum" aria-label="Match customers"><option value="1001">1001 only</option><option value="1002">1001 and 1002</option><option value="1003">All three</option></select></label></div>}
  {kind==='cover'&&<div class="ix-choices"><label class="ix-choice">Index stores <select data-option="variant" aria-label="Index stores"><option value="key">Key only</option><option value="include" selected>Key plus status payload</option><option value="partial">Paid-only key plus status</option></select></label><label class="ix-choice">Row visibility <select data-option="visibility" aria-label="Row visibility"><option value="confirmed">Confirmed without table row</option><option value="check">Needs table-row check</option></select></label></div>}
  <div class="ix-scene" data-scene data-live set:html={first.scene}></div>
  <p class="ix-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{first.explanation}</p>
 </div>
 <div class="ix-controls" role="group" aria-label={`Figure ${number} controls`}><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span><span data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span></div>
 <p class="ix-caption">{caption}</p>
 <details class="ix-text"><summary>All stages, as text</summary>
  {kind==='tree'&&<ol><li>A two-level illustrative B-tree directs customer 1001 through one root to one leaf.</li><li>Its four adjacent entries point to slots (0,1), (1,1), (2,1), (3,1).</li><li>Following them fetches four rows on four table pages. The table has not been reordered.</li></ol>}
  {kind==='keys'&&<p>On these twelve rows, customer-only reads four entries and fetches four rows, checks the date and sorts three eligible rows. Customer, time and ID reads two entries and fetches two rows without sorting. Time first reads six entries, rejects four other customers within the index and fetches two rows without sorting. Each route returns orders 100003 and 100042.</p>}
  {kind==='locality'&&<p>With mixed customers, four, eight or twelve matches reach all four table pages. In customer order, the same matches reach two, three or four pages. Individual fetches can revisit pages. A bitmap route can collect locations and fetch pages in page order; the four-page full scan has no index search. The bars omit index pages and do not measure storage reads.</p>}
  {kind==='cover'&&<p>The paid-only LIMIT 1 request passes November 11 pending, October 25 pending, then October 10 paid. Key-only fetches all three rows. Adding status payload still examines three entries, but needs no table-row fetch when visibility can be confirmed separately. If visibility needs the row, three fetches remain. A paid-only partial index holds just the October 10 entry in this range and examines one; its visibility check can still require that table row.</p>}
 </details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import {frame} from './model.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-index-figure]').forEach((root:HTMLElement)=>{
  const kind=root.dataset.kind!;let options:Record<string,string>={};
  const read=()=>{root.querySelectorAll<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-option]').forEach(s=>options[s.dataset.option!]=s.value);};read();
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:(step:number)=>{const state=frame(kind,step,options);root.querySelector('[data-scene]')!.innerHTML=state.scene;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=state.explanation;}});
  root.querySelectorAll('[data-option]').forEach(s=>s.addEventListener('change',()=>{read();player.render();}));
 });
</script>
